Package: UlavalSSD
Type: Package
Title: Quebec Data and Tools for Introductory Data Science
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Aurélien", "Nicosia", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "nicosia.aurelien@gmail.com")
Description: Historical weather observations and food-establishment conviction
    records from Quebec for teaching data import, missing values, exploratory
    analysis and reproducible reporting. Includes bilingual prompts and feedback
    for a penguin data-cleaning exercise, and an optional static R code-style
    diagnostic based on 'lintr'. Data are distributed as fixed teaching snapshots
    and require no network access during use.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0)
Suggests:
    knitr,
    lintr (>= 3.4.0),
    rmarkdown,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
